# Project-wide line-ending policy.
#
# Every text file lives as CRLF in the working tree AND in the stored
# blob — no `core.autocrlf` flip-flopping per developer, no LF stragglers
# from tools that bypass git's filters (sed, WSL editors, etc.).
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text vs binary by content, so PNG /
# JPG / TGA / fonts / sounds in media/ and libs/ are never line-end
# converted. `eol=crlf` then forces every detected-text file to CRLF on
# both checkout and add.
#
# To bring the index in line with this policy in one shot, run:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git add .gitattributes
* text=auto eol=crlf
